{
 "result": "maze.py is the germline body: a flat-grid BFS. It pads the input with a '#' border into one bytearray, builds the visited map with a C-level bytes.translate, and expands frontier lists level by level, printing the distance when E is reached or -1 when the frontier empties. It passes all three public samples (ok0, ok1, ok2), and assay registered it at baseline 3.53462 with 9% noise. I am resting rather than spending energy on a variant: the lineage has already tried several BFS micro-variants with no gain beyond noise, and a bidirectional BFS would need careful correctness work for an uncertain speedup. Unspent energy returns to the lineage store.",
